+// Package gatefixer owns the life of one cold fixer strand: the agent a failed gate hands its mechanical failures to before the gate is run again.
+//
+// # Roles
+//
+// A fixer strand runs under one of two reed roles, RoleGateFixer for the callers of this package and RoleVerifyFixer for webster's verify-gate fixer.
+// Roles lists them and IsFixerRole reports whether a role, a numbered form included, is one of them.
+//
+// # Record and store
+//
+// A Record is what a caller keeps of one spawned fixer: its strand, session and engine, the spawn time, the shuttle run directory, the events file and the offset past the skill-load turns, and the report and reply paths.
+// It is live while its status is empty, and terminal with StatusDone or StatusDead.
+// The caller owns where records live and reaches them through a Store.
+//
+// # Spawn, wait and stop
+//
+// SpawnOrAttach attaches to the live record a Store holds, and otherwise spawns a strand whose only output file is the reply file, registers it through Deps.Register, and saves its record before it returns.
+// A spawn that cannot be recorded or registered stops the strand again, so no fixer outlives its call unrecorded.
+// Await polls the strand until it is done on its reply file, or dead because its newest turn ended without one, its timeout passed or its strand is gone, and every terminal result stops the strand.
+// Await never marks a record terminal; the caller does.
+// Registrar builds the Deps.Register seam that registers a fixer's pane process with runproc, so runproc's end verbs stop it with the rest of its run.
+//
+// # Prompt
+//
+// RenderPrompt joins one shared cold frame ahead of one caller body stencil, both read through stencilstore at call time, and fills them from the told report and reply paths, the body's own values and the parent, edit, PATTERN and friction directives.
+//
+// # Row gates
+//
+// A Fixer is the spawn-and-wait seam callers drive, and NewStrandFixer is its production form over real strands.
+// WrapRowGate wraps a shuttle gate spec so that a failure of one named entry at the writer's idle boundary goes to a fixer and the entry is judged again over the fixer's finished tree.
+// The wrap keeps its records in a rowStore under the row visit's directory, `<visit dir>/<entry>/records.json`, with each fixer's report and reply beside it as `report-<n>.md` and `reply-<n>.md`.
+// At most one fixer runs per failed evaluation and at most the entry's attempts plus one per row visit, and a failure judged over a fixer the same evaluation waited on goes to the writer.
+// The entry's final closure and every other entry only wait for a live fixer, so every entry is judged over the fixer's finished tree.
+//
+// # Judging
+//
+// A fixer never judges its gate: the caller runs the gate again and that run decides.
+// This package imports nothing of any caller, so every gate caller can import it.
+package gatefixer
diff --git a/internal/gatefixer/fixer.go b/internal/gatefixer/fixer.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e56542db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/gatefixer/fixer.go
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+// fixer.go declares the spawn-and-wait seam a caller drives one cold fixer through, and its production implementation over a strand.
+
+package gatefixer
+
+import "time"
+
+// Fixer is the seam a caller spawns, waits on and stops one cold fixer through, so a test drives the caller over a scripted fixer.
+type Fixer interface {
+	// SpawnOrAttach attaches to the live record store holds, and otherwise spawns a strand under spec and records it in store.
+	// It reports whether this call spawned the fixer.
+	SpawnOrAttach(store Store, spec Spec) (*Record, bool, error)
+	// Await blocks up to wait for rec's fixer to reach a terminal classification, bounding its run by timeout.
+	Await(rec *Record, timeout, wait time.Duration) (*Result, error)
+	// Stop ends rec's strand, and is a no-op for one that is already gone.
+	Stop(rec *Record) error
+}
+
+// strandFixer is the production Fixer over reed strands.
+type strandFixer struct {
+	deps Deps
+}
+
+// NewStrandFixer returns the Fixer that spawns, waits on and stops real fixer strands through deps.
+func NewStrandFixer(deps Deps) Fixer {
+	return strandFixer{deps: deps}
+}
+
+func (f strandFixer) SpawnOrAttach(store Store, spec Spec) (*Record, bool, error) {
+	return SpawnOrAttach(f.deps, store, spec)
+}
+
+func (f strandFixer) Await(rec *Record, timeout, wait time.Duration) (*Result, error) {
+	return Await(f.deps, rec, timeout, wait)
+}
+
+func (f strandFixer) Stop(rec *Record) error {
+	return f.deps.Stopper.StopStrand(rec.StrandGUID)
+}
